 ctrl+p back                                                                │    # flk-run, the run engine (see flk-run for details)                            
                                                                            │    RUN_STOP = "signal:INT"                                                        
                                                                            │    STOP_TIMEOUT = "90"     # then SIGTERM (< kill_timeout)                        
                                                                            │    RESTART_DELAY = "10"    # seconds before restarting after a crash              
                                                                            │    MAX_RESTARTS = "5"      # give up after this many restarts...                  
                                                                            │    RESTART_WINDOW = "600"  # ...within this many seconds                          
                                                                            │                                                                                   
                                                                            │  # The run wrapper restarts the server itself and gives up on a crash loop        
                                                                            │  # (exits 1). flk's restart policy is only the outer net: restart the VM          
                                                                            │  # once, then leave it stopped for a human.                                       
                                                                            │  [[restart]]                                                                      
                                                                            │    policy = "on-failure"                                                          
                                                                            │    retries = 1                                                                    
                                                                            │                                                                                   
                                                                            │  [flk]                                                                            
                                                                            │    keep_releases = 3  # images kept for flk releases rollback (default 2)         
                                                                            │    stdin = "null"     # the app has no console input                              
                                                                            │                                                                                   
                                                                            │  # Backups freeze the VM for the copy (a second or two): the copy holds what      
                                                                            │  # was on disk, like after a power cut. Fine for apps that write atomically       
                                                                            │  # or journal; nobody is disconnected.                                            
─ hint ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 core/backup-live-console: Backups: live, with console save hooks                                                                                               
 Sets [flk.backup] mode = "live" with console pre and post hooks.                                                                                               
 flk volumes backup types each pre line into the app's console (its stdin, the serial console), waits for the wait regex after the last one, then copies the    
 running volume and runs e2fsck on the copy. The post lines run afterwards whatever happened. The console must reach the app: stdin "console" (the default),    
 and a run wrapper that forwards it (flk-run does).                                                                                                             
 ! If the wait line never comes, the backup fails after timeout and the post hooks still run.                                                                   
 ! Not with stdin = "null": the hooks would go nowhere (rule live-backup-console).                                                                              
 More: flk help --all (Config: [flk.backup]); flk help volumes backup                                                                                           
